# Frontend Conventions

React + Vite + TypeScript + shadcn/ui (base-ui), deployed to Firebase Hosting.

## Component Library

Use shadcn/ui for all UI components. These are built on `@base-ui/react`, not Radix.

Key difference from Radix-based shadcn: use `render` prop instead of `asChild`:

```tsx
<DropdownMenuTrigger
  render={<Button variant="ghost"><MoreHorizontal /></Button>}
/>
```

## Multi-Select Pattern

For multi-select fields (clients, marketplaces), use Checkbox-based grids inside a bordered container. Do NOT use Popover or Command patterns:

```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-1.5 rounded-md border p-3">
  {options.map((item) => (
    <label key={item.id} className="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer">
      <Checkbox checked={selected.includes(item.id)} onCheckedChange={() => toggle(item.id)} />
      {item.label}
    </label>
  ))}
</div>
```

## Schedule Data Model

Schedule type uses arrays for multi-select:
- `client_ids: string[]` (not `client_id`)
- `marketplaces: string[]` (not `marketplace`)
- `schedule_config: ScheduleConfig` — flexible scheduling (type, time, days_of_week, day_of_month)
- `folder_name: string` — custom Drive folder
- `subfolder_strategy: "date" | "none"` — subfolder behavior
- `reconciliation_days: number[]` — re-pull days (default [3, 7])

## Firestore Real-Time Data

Use `reactfire` hooks for live data:

```tsx
import { useFirestoreCollectionData } from "reactfire";
import { collection, query, where } from "firebase/firestore";

const jobsQuery = query(collection(firestore, "jobs"), where("status", "==", "running"));
const { data: jobs } = useFirestoreCollectionData(jobsQuery, { idField: "id" });
```

## API Mutations

Use React Query for API calls to the backend:

```tsx
import { useMutation, useQueryClient } from "@tanstack/react-query";

const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL;
const createSchedule = useMutation({
  mutationFn: (data: ScheduleInput) => fetch(`${apiUrl}/schedules`, { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify(data) }),
});
```

## Project Structure

- Pages in `src/pages/`: dashboard, clients, schedules, on-demand
- Shared components in `src/components/`
- Hooks in `src/hooks/`, utilities in `src/lib/`, types in `src/types/`

## Rules

- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` types.
- Prefer named exports over default exports.
- Co-locate component-specific types with the component file.
- Timezone: display all Firestore UTC timestamps using `toLocaleString()` (browser timezone). Never manipulate timezone in the frontend.
